{"r":"h$$","lane":{"p":2894,"e":[{"h":"هَشَّ","t":["aor. ",[2,"يَهِشُّ"],"; (JK, TA;) or ",[2,"هَشَّ"],", secpers. ",[2,"هَشِشْتَ"],", aor. ",[2,"يَهَشُّ"],"; (Msb;) inf. n. ",[2,"هَشَاشَةٌ"]," (JK, A, Msb, TA) [and ",[2,"هُشُوشَةٌ"]," and ",[2,"هُشُوشٌ"]," and ",[2,"هَشٌّ"],", as appears from what follows]; ",[1,"It,"]," (a thing) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, soft, yielding, flaccid, flabby, lax, slack, uncompact, crummy, fragile, frangible, brittle, friable, easily"]," or ",[1,"quickly broken;"]," (JK, A, Msb, TA;) syn. ",[2,"كَانَ فِيهِ رَخَاوَةٌ"],", (JK,) or ",[2,"كَانَ رِخْوًا لَيِّنًا"],", (A, * TA,) or ",[2,"لَانَ وَٱسْتَرْخَى"],". (Msb.) You say, ",[2,"هَشَّ الخُبْزُ"],", aor. , (S, K,) inf. n. ",[2,"هُشُوشَةٌ"]," (K) and ",[2,"هَشٌّ"],", (TA,) meaning, ",[2,"صار"],[2,"هَشًّا"],"; (S, K;) i. e., ",[1,"The bread became"]," [",[1,"soft, &c.,"]," or] ",[1,"easy to break."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"هَشَّ العُودُ"],", (IAar, Msb,) aor. [ , or] , (Msb,) inf. n. ",[2,"هُشُوشٌ"],", (IAar, Msb,) ",[1,"The wood,"]," or ",[1,"stick, broke in pieces:"]," (IAar:) or ",[1,"became easily"]," or ",[1,"quickly broken."]," (Msb.) And ",[2,"هَشَّتِ الشَّجَرَةُ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"هَشٌّ"],", ",[1,"The tree dropped its leaves, one after another."]," (Msb [in which it seems to be indicated that the aor. of the verb in this sense is ; but this is contr. to rule in an intrans. verb of this class; and I think it improbable.]) ― -b2- ",[2,"هَشَّ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"هُشُوشَةٌ"],", (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He"]," (a man) ",[1,"became weak; unable to endure difficulty"]," or ",[1,"distress."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"هَشَّ"],", aor. , (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He affected languor,"]," or ",[1,"languidness;"]," syn. ",[2,"تَكَسَّرَ"],": and ",[1,"he became old,"]," or ",[1,"aged."]," (TA.) -A2- ",[2,"هَشَّ"],", (Msb, K,) first pers. ",[2,"هَشِشْتُ"],", (S, Msb, K,) aor. ",[2,"يَهَشُّ"],"; (Msb, K,) and ",[2,"هَشَّ"],", first pers. ",[2,"هَشَشْتُ"],", aor. ",[2,"يَهِشُّ"],"; (Msb, K;) inf. n. ",[2,"هَشَاشَةٌ"]," (S, Msb, K) and ",[2,"هَشَاشٌ"],"; (A, K;) (tropical:) ",[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, cheerful, brisk, lively,"]," or ",[1,"sprightly:"]," (S, K:) or ",[1,"he smiled, and was,"]," or ",[1,"became cheerful, brisk, lively,"]," or ",[1,"sprightly."]," (Msb.) You say, ",[2,"هَشِشْتُ بِفُلَانٍ"],", (S, TA,) and ",[2,"هَشَشْتُ بِهِ"],", (TA,) (tropical:) ",[1,"I was,"]," or ",[1,"became, cheerful,"]," &c. ",[1,"in behaviour towards such a one:"]," (S:) or ",[1,"I was,"]," or ",[1,"became cheerful in countenance,"]," or ",[1,"joyful,"]," or ",[1,"pleased, at meeting with such a one."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"هُوَ يَهَشُّ إِلَى إِخْوَانِهِ"],", (tropical:) ",[1,"He is cheerful,"]," &c., ",[1,"towards his brethren"],"]. (A.) And ",[2,"بِى"]," ↓ ",[2,"دَخَلْتُ عَلَيْهِ فَٱهْتَشَّ"]," (tropical:) [",[1,"I went in to him, and he was cheerful,"]," &c., ",[1,"in his behaviour towards me"],"]; like ",[2,"إِهْتَزَّ لى"],". (A, * TA.) And ",[2,"هَشِشْتُ لِلْمَعْرُوفِ"],", (JK, TA, *) and ",[2,"هَشَشْتُ"],", (TA,) inf. n. ",[2,"هَشَاشَةٌ"]," (S) and ",[2,"هَشَاشٌ"],", (A,) (tropical:) ",[1,"I was,"]," or ",[1,"became, cheerful, brisk,"]," &c., ",[1,"to do what was kind,"]," or ",[1,"beneficent:"]," (S, * TA:) or ",[1,"I desired to do it:"]," (JK:) and ↓ ",[2,"إِهْتَشَشْتُ"],[2,"للمعروف"],[1,"I was,"]," or ",[1,"became, cheerful,"]," &c., ",[1,"and desirous, to do what was kind,"]," or ",[1,"beneficent."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"هُوَ ذُو هَشَاشٍ إِلَى الخَيْرِ"]," (tropical:) [",[1,"He possesses cheerfulness, briskness, liveliness,"]," or ",[1,"sprightliness, of disposition to do good"],"]. (A.) Accord. to Sh, ",[2,"هَشِشْتُ"]," signifies (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He rejoiced, and desired;"]," or ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, joyful, and desirous."]," (TA.) And the phrase ",[2,"هَشِشْتُ إِلَى ٱمْرَأَتِى"],", if correct, means either (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"I inclined towards my wife,"]," or ",[1,"I was,"]," or ",[1,"became, brisk,"]," or ",[1,"sprightly, in disposition towards her."]," (Mgh.) And accord to ISd, ",[2,"هَشَاشُ القَوْمِ"]," [so in the TA, but accord. to the JK ",[2,"هَشَاهِشُ"],",] (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The people's being in a state of commotion,"]," or ",[1,"agitation."]," (TA.) -A3- ",[2,"هَشَّ الوَرَقَ"],", aor. , (S, A, K,) and , (Sgh, K,) inf. n. ",[2,"هَشٌّ"],", (S,) ",[1,"He beat the leaves"]," with a staff, or stick, ",[1,"in order that they might fall;"]," (S, A, K;) as also ↓ ",[2,"هَشْهَشَهُ"],". (Z, TA.) It is said in the Kur, [xx. 19,] (S,) ",[2,"وَأَهُشُّ بِهَا عَلَى غَنَمِى"]," [",[1,"And I beat the leaves with it in order that they may fall upon my sheep,"]," or ",[1,"goats"],"]: (S, A:) or, accord. to Fr, ",[1,"and I beat the dry trees with it in order that their leaves may fall so that my sheep,"]," or ",[1,"goats, may feed upon them;"]," and so says As: (TA:) Lth says, that ",[2,"الهَشُّ"]," signifies thy ",[1,"drawing towards thee a branch of a tree:"]," and also, thy ",[1,"scattering its leaves towards thee with a staff,"]," or ",[1,"stick:"]," (JK, * TA:) but Az says, that the correct ex- planation is that given by Fr and As; not the former of the two explanations given by Lth. (TA.) [The verb also seems to have a similar application in a more extended sense; for it is said that] ",[2,"هَشَّ"],", aor. , inf. n. ",[2,"هَشٌّ"],", signifies He (a man) assaulted (",[2,"صَالَ"],") with his staff, or stick. (Msb.) You say also, ",[2,"هَشَّ الهَشِيمَ"],[1,"He broke in pieces the dry herbage"]," or ",[1,"the like."]," (TA.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"هشّشهُ","t":["(JK, K,) inf. n. ",[2,"تَهْشِيشٌ"],", (TA,) (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He deemed him,"]," or ",[1,"reckoned him, weak,"]," or ",[1,"feeble,"]," (JK, K, *) ",[1,"and soft,"]," or ",[1,"gentle."]," (TA.) -A2- (tropical:) ",[1,"He,"]," or ",[1,"it, rendered him brisk, lively,"]," or ",[1,"sprightly; and joyful, glad,"]," or ",[1,"happy:"]," (K:) and ↓ ",[2,"استهشّهُ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"it"]," (a thing, JK, TA) ",[1,"incited him,"]," or ",[1,"excited him, to briskness, liveliness"]," or ",[1,"sprightliness;"]," syn. ",[2,"إِسْتَخَفَّهُ"],". (JK, K, TA.) You say, ↓ ",[2,"فُلَانٌ مَا يَسْتَهِشُّهُ"],[2,"النَّعِيمُ"]," (tropical:) [",[1,"Such a one, weal,"]," or ",[1,"welfare, does not excite him to briskness,"]," &c.] (A, TA.)"],"f":"2"},{"h":"اهتشّ","t":[[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, cheerful,"]," &c.: see 1, in two places."],"f":"8"},{"h":"إِسْتَهْشَ3َ","t":["see 2, in two places."],"f":"10"},{"h":"هَشْهَشَهُ","t":[": see 1, latter part. ― -b2- ",[1,"He moved,"]," or ",[1,"put in motion,"]," or ",[1,"into a state of commotion, him, or it."]," (IDrd, K.)"],"f":"R. Q. 1"},{"h":"هَشٌّ","t":["A thing, (S, Msb,) or anything, (JK,) ",[1,"soft, yielding, flaccid, flabby, lax, slack, uncompact, crummy, fragile, frangible, brittle, friable, easily"]," or ",[1,"quickly broken;"]," (JK, * S, * A, * Msb, K, * TA;) syn. ",[2,"رِخْوٌ لَيِّنٌ"],"; (S, A, K;) as also ↓ ",[2,"هَشِيشٌ"],". (JK, S, K.) You say, ",[2,"خُبْزٌ هَشٌّ"],", (S, K,) and ↓ ",[2,"هَشَاشٌ"],", (K,) ",[1,"Bread that is"]," [",[1,"soft,"]," &c., or] ",[1,"easy to break."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"خُبْزَةٌ هَشَّةٌ"],[1,"A lump of dough, baked in a fire in the ground, that is dry,"]," or ",[1,"hard:"]," asserted by IKtt to have two contr. significations. (TA.) [But to this assertion it may be replied, that dry bread is easy to break.] And in like manner, ",[2,"أُتْرُجَّةٌ هَشَّةٌ"],[1,"A citron easy to break:"]," or ",[1,"dry,"]," or ",[1,"hard."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"عُودٌ هَشٌّ"],[1,"Wood,"]," or ",[1,"a stick, that is easily,"]," or ",[1,"quickly broken."]," (Msb.) ― -b2- [Hence,] ",[2,"هُوَ هَشٌّ"],[2,"المَكْسِرِ"],", (JK, S, A, K,) or ",[2,"المَكْسَرِ"],", (TA, [but this is contr. to all the other authorities that I know,]) and ",[2,"المُكَسَّرِ"],", (TA,) (tropical:) ",[1,"He is easy,"]," or ",[1,"compliant, when asked:"]," (A:) or ",[1,"he is of easy nature,"]," or ",[1,"disposition,"]," (JK, S, K,) ",[1,"with respect to what is sought,"]," or ",[1,"demanded, of him,